<h2>Asobi Review 1.0.1 (build 2226) <span class="when">Nov 11, 2026</span></h2>
<ul>
<li><b>Push a grade to the room.</b> In a live review, expert reviewers can send their grade on a clip to everyone, or put it on every clip, from the new icon in the grade panel. Other reviewers ask the host, who can allow it once or for the rest of the review.</li>
</ul>
<hr>
<div class="earlier">Earlier updates</div>
<h3>1.0 (build 2215) <span class="when">Nov 10, 2026</span></h3>
<ul>
<li><b>Clips the host removes leave your playlist too</b> during a live review, instead of staying on your screen.</li>
</ul>
<h3>1.0 (build 2211) <span class="when">Nov 10, 2026</span></h3>
<ul>
<li><b>Showcases show what they're doing</b> while the picture is prepared, and the bar keeps moving instead of sitting at halfway.</li>
</ul>
<h3>1.0 (build 2208) <span class="when">Nov 9, 2026</span></h3>
<ul>
<li><b>Playlist actions on a right-click.</b> What was in the playlist's More menu is now on a right-click of the footer, a movie's header or any row.</li>
<li><b>Closing a floating panel</b> puts it back in the side panel and shows it.</li>
</ul>
<h3>1.0 (build 2205) <span class="when">Nov 9, 2026</span></h3>
<ul>
<li><b>Menus that closed by themselves</b> (the playlist's More, the color chip) open and stay open again.</li>
<li><b>Progress header</b> in the Notes column fits instead of being cut off.</li>
</ul>
<h3>1.0 (build 2199) <span class="when">Nov 9, 2026</span></h3>
<ul>
<li><b>As on this Mac.</b> A new first choice in the color chip's Footage menu: the picture looks as it does in Preview or QuickTime Player. Stills start this way.</li>
<li><b>Rejoining a big review.</b> Joining a review with a lot in it could fail with "Message too long". Fixed.</li>
<li><b>Undo for the playlist</b>, and Sort ▸ Cut Order to put a cut movie's shots back in order.</li>
</ul>
<h3>1.0 (build 2191) <span class="when">Nov 9, 2026</span></h3>
<ul>
<li><b>A Kitsu tab in Notes,</b> off unless turned on in Settings ▸ Interface.</li>
</ul>
<h3>1.0 (build 2186) <span class="when">Nov 9, 2026</span></h3>
<ul>
<li><b>Frame.io comments come back with their authors' names and drawings.</b></li>
<li><b>The Progress view shows the agency's latest comments.</b></li>
</ul>
]]></description>
